From: viettatlahkd <314170691+viettatlahkd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:39:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: the breadcrumbs in admin were a caption, not a trail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every crumb on every admin screen was a label with no handler — Admin, Backend,
Notes, Templates, none of them went anywhere. The bar read like a way back and
was a picture of one, so the only way out was the sidebar or the browser's own
button.

A crumb that names a page it can reach now carries it. Backend and Notes name
groupings rather than pages, so they point at where their group starts, Content
management. And the back arrow stayed inside admin: from Templates it used to
leave the area entirely and land on the public journal, which is not one step
back from anywhere.

A test walks all nine screens and asserts every crumb but the last one goes
somewhere. The last is the page being looked at and stays put.

The "← mọi template" link stays. It looks like a duplicate of the trail and is
not: opening a template does not change screen, so the Templates crumb is still
the current page and cannot return from a template to the list. Making the
trail own that step means putting the open template in the URL, which is a
larger change than this one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
